ndscape maintenance tasks important to the preservation, protection, and display of landscape beds, including but not limited to soil preparation, planting, transplanting, mulching, weeding, irrigation, fertilizing, pesticide/herbicide applications, tree work etc.. Maintains care of tools, equipment and university property. Exercises quality mowing, string trimming, and... View Details Bookmark Public Safety Telecommunicator - cert req'd - 2826 SPA00754 Police & Public Safety SHRA 09/09/2026 Police Dispatcher Call Intake & AssessmentAnswer emergency and non-emergency phone calls promptly and professionally.Receive and respond to emergency and non-emergency requests for assistance through non-telephonic communication means, such as callboxes, panic buttons, Brave Alert messages, etc.Assess caller needs, obtain essential information, and determine the appropriate level of response.Provide pre-arri... View Details Bookmark Accounting Technician - 43 SPA00753 Bursar SHRA 09/09/2026 Student Account Analyst This position’s duties include administering, developing, and monitoring student accounts. The impact from tasks performed and contacts made by this position is university-wide and the responsibilities require, analytical thinking, the application of sound judgments, independent decisions making ability, time management and the ability to establish personal contacts and to successfully communic... View Details Bookmark Student Services Specialist - 2912 SPA00752 Financial Aid SHRA 09/09/2026 Financial Aid Counselor The counselor will be responsible for counseling students about the amount of financial aid that they can receive, including eligibility for federal, state and institutional grants and loans. Each counselor will be responsible for counseling a portion of the student population on aid which is divided by alphabet. Part of this job includes counseling student about Satisfactory Academic Progress.... View Details Bookmark Student Services Specialist - 410 SPA00751 Financial Aid SHRA 09/09/2026 FA Counselor/Scholarship Coordinator DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES:This position is responsible for coordinating the university’s major scholarship initiatives, determining student eligibility, and counseling students, parents, faculty, and staff regarding scholarships, financial aid opportunities, and navigation of the system. The counselor will continuously evaluate the University’s scholarship program identifying opportunities fo... View Details Bookmark Sponsored Programs Specialist - 3530 EPA01166 Sponsored Research & Programs EHRA Sponsored Programs Specialist The Sponsored Programs Specialist (SPS) is responsible for supporting campus departments, sponsors, and subrecipients in a fast-paced, high volume team environment for the submission of proposals for extramurally funded projects on behalf of UNCP.The work performed by the Sponsored Programs Specialist (SPS) requires an understanding of the types of proposals and grant mechanisms used by funding... View Details Bookmark Facilities Superintendent - 3280 EPA01165 Facilities Operations EHRA Facilities Superintendent This position manages the division of Grounds, Housekeeping, Event Set-Ups and Labor, as well as asset management for the Division of Facilities Operations and Maintenance. Position oversees all technical services provided by staff, organizes and plans work, supervises the work and career development of staff, manages the facilities budget, and participates in strategic planning. Interview pros... View Details Bookmark Study Abroad Coordinator -2528 EPA01164 Office of Global Engagement EHRA Study Abroad Coordinator - 2528 70%: This position is primarily responsible for recruitment of UNCP study abroad/away students, balancing exchange-in-kind with incoming exchange students, direct exchanges, exchanges in conjunction with consortiums, and faculty-led programs. This position has budget responsibility for faculty-led programs, scholarship awards and financial aid. The Study Abroad Coordinator is responsible for im... View Details Bookmark Kinesiology Adjuncts (2026-27) NP00404 Department of Kinesiology Temporary Employment Kinesiology Adjuncts (2026-27) The Department of Kinesiology is in need of a candidate that can teach in person with some occasional online options in the summer. Applicants must have a minimum of a master’s (but preference is given to those holding doctoral degrees) from an accredited college/ university in Kinesiology or a related sub-discipline. Those teaching at the graduate level would be expected to hold doctorate in t... View Details Bookmark Sr. Police Supervisor I - 1430 EPA01146 Police & Public Safety EHRA Lieutenant Job Description | The Lieutenant (Senior Police Supervisor) reports to the Assistant Chief of Police (Police Commander). This position provides daily mid-level management and supervisory oversight to one of the department’s functional divisions. The Lieutenant may provide direct supervision to sworn police supervisors (Sergeants) and non-sworn supervisors and personnel. The Lieutenant will be r... View Details Bookmark Sr. Police Supervisor I - 3211 EPA01081 Police & Public Safety EHRA Lieutenant - 3211 The Lieutenant (Senior Police Supervisor) reports to the Assistant Chief of Police (Police Commander). This position provides daily mid-level management and supervisory oversight to one of the department’s functional divisions. The Lieutenant may provide direct supervision to sworn police supervisors (Sergeants) and non-sworn supervisors and personnel. The Lieutenant will be responsible for man... View Details Bookmark Theatre Adjuncts (2026-2027) NP00403 English, Theatre & Languages (Office) Temporary Employment Theatre Adjuncts (2026-2027) The Department of English, Theatre, and World Languages seeks adjunct faculty to teach face-to-face undergraduate Theatre courses. Applicants must have a PhD in Theatre Studies or a Master’s Degree in Theatre or MFA or other terminal degree in Theatre or a closely related field that includes a minimum of 18 graduate credit hours in Theatre. All degrees must come from accredited institutions. St... View Details Bookmark Assistant Professor, Social Work - 3259 EPA01083 Social Work EHRA Assistant Professor, Social Work - 3259 The Department of Social Work has both BSW and MSW programs. Programs include advanced standing, part-time and night/evening, on-campus and online. The successful candidate will be required to teach 6-8 courses per academic year (courses may include field seminar and field supervision); develop curricula; provide academic advisement to current and prospective students; maintain an active progra... View Details Bookmark Instructional Services Reference Librarian - 2457 EPA01121 Library Services EHRA Instructional Services Reference Librarian - 2457 1. Supervise library technician(s) within in the instruction department.2. Develop and maintain online learning materials for the library with an understanding of learning management systems, Open Education Resources initiatives, LibGuides, AI, digital repositories, and innovative digital tools.3. Design collaborative material for librarians with instruction duties, including Instructional Reso... View Details Bookmark Assistant Professor of Criminal Justice - 3505 EPA01163 Sociology & Criminal Jus. EHRA Assistant Professor of Criminal Justice - 3505 The Department of Sociology and Criminal Justice at the University of North Carolina at Pembroke invites applications for a tenure track Assistant Professor of Criminal Justice position to begin in the fall of 2027.The University of North Carolina at Pembroke is one of the seventeen member institutions in the University of North Carolina system. The Department of Sociology and Criminal Justice ... View Details Bookmark Assistant Professor of Sociology and Criminal Justice - 3419 EPA01162 Sociology & Criminal Jus. EHRA Assistant Professor of Sociology and Criminal Justice - 3419 The Department of Sociology and Criminal Justice at the University of North Carolina at Pembroke invites applications for a tenure track Assistant Professor of Sociology and Criminal Justice position to begin in the fall of 2027.The University of North Carolina at Pembroke is one of the seventeen member institutions in the University of North Carolina system. The Department of Sociology and Cri... View Details Bookmark Assistant Professor of Sociology - 811 EPA01161 Sociology & Criminal Jus. EHRA Assistant Professor of Sociology - 811 The Department of Sociology and Criminal Justice at the University of North Carolina at Pembroke invites applications for a tenure track Assistant Professor of Sociology position to begin in the fall of 2027.The University of North Carolina at Pembroke is one of the seventeen member institutions in the University of North Carolina system. The Department of Sociology and Criminal Justice is grow... View Details Bookmark Building Environmental Services Manager II - 2652 EPA01159 Facilities Operations EHRA Grounds Manager II - 2652 Grounds Manager (EHRA) – Position DescriptionThe Grounds Manager provides strategic leadership and administrative oversight for all campus grounds and athletic field operations at the University of North Carolina at Pembroke. This position is responsible for the planning, development, and execution of comprehensive grounds management programs that support the University’s academic, residential,... View Details Bookmark Macroeconomics Adjuncts (2026-2027) NP00402 Economics, Marketing, Entrepreneurship and Analytics (EMEA) Temporary Employment Macroeconomics Adjuncts (2026-2027) The ideal candidate shall be willing to teach undergraduate level courses in the area of macroeconomics, including Principles of Macroeconomics.The successful applicant will teach courses in the college’s undergraduate programs.Application Instructions: Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled.Please contact the Department Chair, Daniel J. Parisian... View Details Bookmark Associate Vice Chancellor of Student Success - 2952 EPA01144 Academic Affairs Dept EHRA Associate Vice Chancellor of Student Success Please view our Senior Leadership Profile.The Associate Vice Chancellor for Student Success will provide strategic leadership for campus-wide student success initiatives and integrated academic support services that support students from admission through graduation. The position’s primary focus is on advancing student success through data-informed decision making, coordinated advising and supp... View Details Bookmark Police Officer - 3340 EPA01152 Police & Public Safety EHRA Police Officer - 3340 Responds and/or investigates complaints and violations of the law to determine the causes, to identify witnesses, and to preserve evidence through crime scene search; arrests suspects and testifies in court; and completes reports of incidents and cases.Patrols the University’s parking lots, streets, grounds and buildings to enforce the law and to ensure the protection and safety of persons and ... View Details Bookmark Assistant/Associate Professor Public Administration - 2403 EPA01158 Political Science & Public Admin EHRA Assistant/Associate Professor Public Administration - 2403 Associate or Assistant Professor of Public AdministrationThe Department of Political Science and Public Administration at the University of North Carolina at Pembroke seeks an associate or assistant professor of public administration with the ability to teach courses in public budgeting and finance at the graduate and undergraduate level in addition to other courses in the discipline. This posi... View Details Bookmark Sponsored Programs Specialist - 2588 EPA01079 Sponsored Research & Programs EHRA Sponsored Programs Specialist - 2588 The work performed by the Sponsored Projects Specialist (SPS) requires an understanding of the types of proposals and grant mechanisms used by funding agencies; the processes for application submission; and the terms and conditions of each request for proposal. This knowledge is necessary in order to communicate rules, regulations, and procedures to faculty members, staff, and stakeholders, as ... View Details Bookmark Human Resources Consultant - 360 EPA01155 Office of Human Resources EHRA Human Resources Consultant - 360 Founded in 1887 as a school for the education of American Indians, The University of North Carolina Pembroke (UNCP) now serves a robust student body. UNCP exists to promote excellence in teaching and learning, in bachelor’s, master’s and professional doctoral degrees, in an environment of free inquiry, interdisciplinary collaboration and rigorous intellectual standards. As a constituent institu... View Details Bookmark Adjunct Faculty/Master Occupational Therapy 2026-2027 NP00400 Department of Occupational Therapy Temporary Employment Adjunct Faculty/Master Occupational Therapy 2026-2027 Established in 1887 as a school for the education of American Indians, The University of North Carolina at Pembroke serves a distinctly diverse student body and encourages inclusion and appreciation of the values of all people. Located in the heart of Pembroke, N.C., UNCP boasts an enrollment of 8,200 in 41 undergraduate and 18 graduate programs and offers a personalized learning environment wh... View Details Bookmark Accounting and Finance Adjunct Professor (2026-2027) NP00399 Accounting, Finance & Information Technology Management (AFIT) Temporary Employment Accounting and Finance Adjunct Professor (2026-2027) Teach online/ face-to-face, graduate/undergraduate level courses in accounting and finance such as financial accounting, managerial accounting. business finance, personal finance, trading, investments etc.The Accounting, Finance & Information Technology Management Department has a strong commitment to undergraduate teaching and part-time faculty are expected to exhibit and maintain campus a... View Details Bookmark Business Law Adjunct (2026-2027) NP00398 Accounting, Finance & Information Technology Management (AFIT) Temporary Employment Business Law Adjunct (2026-2027) The Department of Accounting and Finance commonly has the need for a part-time faculty to teach Business Law & Ethics courses in the 2026-2027 academic year.Teach online/ face-to-face, graduate/undergraduate level courses in business law such as legal and ethical issues, legal issues for managers, legal and ethical issues for health care professionals, international business law etc.The Acc... View Details Bookmark Management Adjuncts (2026 - 2027) NP00388 Management, International Business and Supply Chain Management (MIBS) Temporary Employment Management Adjuncts (2026 - 2027) Established in 1887 as a school for the education of American Indians, The University of North Carolina at Pembroke serves a distinctly diverse student body and encourages inclusion and appreciation of the values of all people. Located in the heart of Pembroke, N.C., UNCP boasts an enrollment of 7,500 in 41 undergraduate and 18 graduate programs and offers a personalized learning environment wh... View Details Bookmark Go to search results page: Previous 1 2 Next CAMPUS DIRECTORY | ASK UNCP | UNIVERSITY CALENDAR To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
