y to teach courses in core and specialty areas for Professional School Counseling and Clinical Mental Health Counseling.We invite applications to be submitted for potential openings.These positions are especially suited for potential faculty who possess a doctorate in Counselor Education and Supervision and independent licensu... View Details Bookmark Deputy Provost - 3503 EPA01156 Academic Affairs Dept EHRA Deputy Provost - 3503 The Deputy Provost provides leadership for divisional strategic planning, operational management, academic business processes, policy oversight, institutional reporting, and coordination of initiatives associated with the University’s Academic Strategic Plan. Acting with delegated authority on behalf of the Provost, the Deputy Provost works closely with Associate Vice Chancellors, Deans, depart... View Details Bookmark English Composition Adjuncts (2026-2027) NP00390 English, Theatre & Languages (Office) Temporary Employment English Composition Adjuncts (2026-2027) The Department of English, Theatre, and World Languages seeks adjunct faculty to teach face-to-face courses in Composition I and Composition II. Applicants must have a PhD in English or a master’s degree in English or a related field that includes a minimum of 18 hours of graduate work in English. All degrees must come from accredited institutions. Strong consideration will be afforded to candi... View Details Bookmark Environmental Health and Safety Professional - 3487 SPA00756 Emergency Operations SHRA 09/15/2026 Environmental Health and Safety Professional Promote Occupational Health and Safety (OH&S) within all UNCP facilities and represent management in Occupational Health and Safety matters. Conducts annual school/building inspections and prepares and distributes inspection reports; including follow-up activities.Responds to all emergency inspections and requests and reports to committees and management. Investigates and makes recommendati... View Details Bookmark Student Services Specialist - 410 SPA00751 Financial Aid SHRA 09/09/2026 FA Counselor/Scholarship Coordinator DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES:This position is responsible for coordinating the university’s major scholarship initiatives, determining student eligibility, and counseling students, parents, faculty, and staff regarding scholarships, financial aid opportunities, and navigation of the system. The counselor will continuously evaluate the University’s scholarship program identifying opportunities fo... View Details Bookmark Facilities Superintendent - 3280 EPA01165 Facilities Operations EHRA Facilities Superintendent This position manages the division of Grounds, Housekeeping, Event Set-Ups and Labor, as well as asset management for the Division of Facilities Operations and Maintenance. Position oversees all technical services provided by staff, organizes and plans work, supervises the work and career development of staff, manages the facilities budget, and participates in strategic planning. Interview pros... View Details Bookmark Student Services Specialist - 2912 SPA00752 Financial Aid SHRA 09/09/2026 Financial Aid Counselor The counselor will be responsible for counseling students about the amount of financial aid that they can receive, including eligibility for federal, state and institutional grants and loans. Each counselor will be responsible for counseling a portion of the student population on aid which is divided by alphabet. Part of this job includes counseling student about Satisfactory Academic Progress.... View Details Bookmark Building Environmental Services Manager II - 2652 EPA01159 Facilities Operations EHRA Grounds Manager II - 2652 Grounds Manager (EHRA) – Position DescriptionThe Grounds Manager provides strategic leadership and administrative oversight for all campus grounds and athletic field operations at the University of North Carolina at Pembroke. This position is responsible for the planning, development, and execution of comprehensive grounds management programs that support the University’s academic, residential,... View Details Bookmark Human Resources Consultant - 360 EPA01155 Office of Human Resources EHRA Human Resources Consultant - 360 Founded in 1887 as a school for the education of American Indians, The University of North Carolina Pembroke (UNCP) now serves a robust student body. UNCP exists to promote excellence in teaching and learning, in bachelor’s, master’s and professional doctoral degrees, in an environment of free inquiry, interdisciplinary collaboration and rigorous intellectual standards. As a constituent institu... View Details Bookmark Instructional Services Reference Librarian - 2457 EPA01121 Library Services EHRA Instructional Services Reference Librarian - 2457 1. Supervise library technician(s) within in the instruction department.2. Develop and maintain online learning materials for the library with an understanding of learning management systems, Open Education Resources initiatives, LibGuides, AI, digital repositories, and innovative digital tools.3. Design collaborative material for librarians with instruction duties, including Instructional Reso... View Details Bookmark Kinesiology Adjuncts (2026-27) NP00404 Department of Kinesiology Temporary Employment Kinesiology Adjuncts (2026-27) The Department of Kinesiology is in need of a candidate that can teach in person with some occasional online options in the summer. Applicants must have a minimum of a master’s (but preference is given to those holding doctoral degrees) from an accredited college/ university in Kinesiology or a related sub-discipline. Those teaching at the graduate level would be expected to hold doctorate in t... View Details Bookmark Sr. Police Supervisor I - 1430 EPA01146 Police & Public Safety EHRA Lieutenant Job Description | The Lieutenant (Senior Police Supervisor) reports to the Assistant Chief of Police (Police Commander). This position provides daily mid-level management and supervisory oversight to one of the department’s functional divisions. The Lieutenant may provide direct supervision to sworn police supervisors (Sergeants) and non-sworn supervisors and personnel. The Lieutenant will be r... View Details Bookmark Sr. Police Supervisor I - 3211 EPA01081 Police & Public Safety EHRA Lieutenant - 3211 The Lieutenant (Senior Police Supervisor) reports to the Assistant Chief of Police (Police Commander). This position provides daily mid-level management and supervisory oversight to one of the department’s functional divisions. The Lieutenant may provide direct supervision to sworn police supervisors (Sergeants) and non-sworn supervisors and personnel. The Lieutenant will be responsible for man... View Details Bookmark Macroeconomics Adjuncts (2026-2027) NP00402 Economics, Marketing, Entrepreneurship and Analytics (EMEA) Temporary Employment Macroeconomics Adjuncts (2026-2027) The ideal candidate shall be willing to teach undergraduate level courses in the area of macroeconomics, including Principles of Macroeconomics.The successful applicant will teach courses in the college’s undergraduate programs.Application Instructions: Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled.Please contact the Department Chair, Daniel J. Parisian... View Details Bookmark Go to search results page: Previous 1 2 Next CAMPUS DIRECTORY | ASK UNCP | UNIVERSITY CALENDAR To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
