    "https://jobs.uncp.edu/postings/13530": {
      "title": "Human Resources",
      "description": "University of North Carolina Pembroke Applicant Portal | Human Resources Consultant - 360 Skip to Main Content UNCP home Human Resources Human Resources Visit Us Request Info Apply UNCP Home About UNC Pembroke Human Resources Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help UNCP Home Contact Us Human Resources Consultant - 360 Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. This position is subject to the successful completion of an employment background check. An employment background check includes a criminal background check, employment verification, reference checks, license verification (if applicable) and credit history check (if applicable). In compliance with federal law, all persons hired will be required to verify identity and eligibility to work in the United States and to complete the required employment eligibility verification form upon hire. New employees are paid only by direct deposit to the financial institution of their choice. Candidates claiming Veterans Preference must attach a copy of their DD-214 as a part of the online application process. UNC Pembroke is an Equal Opportunity Employer. The University prohibits discrimination against qualified individuals based on their status as protected veterans or individuals with disabilities, and prohibits discrimination against all individuals based on their age, race, color, genetic information, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression and national origin. UNC Pembroke is a VEVRAA Federal Contractor and seeks priority referrals of protected veterans for our openings. Position Details Position Information Division Chancellor's Office Department Office of Human Resources Working Title Human Resources Consultant - 360 Vacancy Type Exempt Professional Staff (EPS) Min T/E Requirements Bachelor’s degree and two years of progressively responsible professional human resources experience; or an equivalent combination of training and experience. All degrees must be from appropriately accredited institutions. FTE 1.0 Recruitment Range Commensurate Upon Education and Experience Anticipated Hiring Range Commensurate Upon Education and Experience Position # 360 FLSA Status Exempt Months per year 12 Is this a grant funded position? No If yes, please indicate the end date of the grant.(if applicable) . Primary Purpose of Organization Unit The position is part of the University’s Office of Human Resources, within the Chancellor’s Division. The department provides a wide range of customer-focused HR services, including: Recruitment and employment for all university positions, including EHRA faculty, non-faculty, SHRA , Exempt Professional Staff ( EPS ), temporary and student employees EEO compliance, classification and salary administration Performance management, professional development, and training Records management, policy and procedural administration Employee relations, HR information systems & data reporting These services comply with guidelines from the University of North Carolina system’s UNC Policy Manual The Code, the N.C. Office of State Human Resources, and federal and state laws. The department supports nearly 900 benefits-eligible staff, and approximately 300 temporary employees and students. Primary Purpose of Position The primary purpose of the Human Resources Consultant is to support the department of Facilities Management (Operations, Maintenance, Planning, Construction and Design), by providing overall leadership and management for all human resources/personnel matters. This position is responsible for maintaining confidentiality of all information, understanding and communicating policies, procedures, and guidelines, and recommending solutions as an extension of the Office of Human Resources. Job Description Founded in 1887 as a school for the education of American Indians, The University of North Carolina Pembroke ( UNCP ) now serves a robust student body. UNCP exists to promote excellence in teaching and learning, in bachelor’s, master’s and professional doctoral degrees, in an environment of free inquiry, interdisciplinary collaboration and rigorous intellectual standards. As a constituent institution of the 17-campus University of North Carolina System, UNCP is known for small classes, close interaction with faculty, and community involvement. UNCP is a campus where faculty and staff meet every individual student where they are with the tools needed to succeed. A student-faculty ratio of 14:1 and an average class size of 17 create a context for personalized teaching, learning and research. Nestled in the heart of picturesque landscapes, Pembroke stands as a testament to the harmonious blend of history, culture, and nature. Our town offers an array of activities and experiences waiting to be explored. From our historic landmarks, lush parks, and bustling local markets to our tight-knit community events, there’s something for everyone here. UNCP is consistently one of the safest campuses in the University of North Carolina System. The university is proud to serve its entire community including nontraditional, first-generation and military-affiliated students. At the University of North Carolina Pembroke, we are dedicated to fostering excellence in education and research. Employees (benefits eligible) of UNCP receive a comprehensive benefits package along with various programs, resources, policies, and practices aimed at supporting a healthy work/life balance. Our offerings are designed to provide a range of choices to meet both the employee and their family’s needs. Permanent, full-time employees (benefits eligible) qualify for dental, vision, and health insurance plans. Eligibility for health insurance benefits begins on the first of the month following the date of hire. Retirement plan contributions start on the eligibility date after the employee election and include employer contributions to either a defined contribution or defined benefit plan. Additionally, optional disability plans, supplemental retirement plans, and pre-tax flexible spending accounts are available. Benefits eligible employees are also eligible to participate in the university’s tuition waiver program, which covers the cost of tuition and fees for up to three (3) undergraduate or graduate courses per academic year at UNCP or any institution within The University of North Carolina system. Permanent, full-time employees (benefits eligible) enjoy 12 paid holidays and, if eligible, receive 24 hours of paid community service leave, as well as accruals for vacation, personal leave, and sick leave as applicable. Family medical leave ( FMLA ) and paid parental leave is available after 12 months of continuous service. The office of Human Resources, takes pride in serving our faculty and staff to promote pathways that help our students and employees find success. We are looking for a passionate and highly qualified individual to join us! Job Duties and Responsibilities: The Human Resources (HR) Consultant serves as a strategic human resources partner primarily supporting the Facilities Management department (Operations, Maintenance, Planning, Construction and Design) providing expert-level guidance and operational support across a broad range of HR functions. This position’s primary responsibility is to manage training and professional development initiatives, full-cycle recruitment, performance management, and disciplinary processes. The HR Consultant works closely with leaders, supervisors, staff professionals, and the Office of Human Resources ( OHR ) to advance university and strategic initiatives and uphold the university’s commitment to effective people management. This position will serve as an extension of the Office of Human Resources with a primary location in the Facilities Management department and is responsible for maintaining strict confidentiality of all information, communicating policies, procedures, and guidelines, and collaborating directly on all personnel matters with OHR leadership. Key responsibilities include: Workforce Relations Management – 30% Serve as the primary on-site HR point of contact for Facilities Management leadership and staff, functioning as an embedded extension of the Office of Human Resources while maintaining alignment with university, State, and UNC System policies, priorities, and leadership direction Manage employee relations, including coaching supervisors, facilitating disciplinary processes, and resolving personnel matters in accordance with OSHR , UNC System The Code, and university policy and procedures Serve as a subject matter expert on human resources policies and procedures — interpreting, communicating, and implementing both internal university policies and applicable state and federal regulations Ensure departmental compliance with all personnel-related policies, procedures, and legal requirements; identify and proactively address compliance gaps Process all SHRA and EHRA personnel actions following initiation by the supervisor Develop and maintain position descriptions and vacancy notices; route personnel actions initiated by the supervisor through appropriate approval channels Coordinate all employment and separation processes for employees across all classifications, ensuring accuracy, timeliness, and compliance at each stage, in consultation with the Director of Workforce Development and Employee Relations Training and Development – 25% Lead the design, development, and delivery of customized training programs addressing performance management, disciplinary processes, human resources policy compliance, and professional development for supervisors and staff Assess departmental training needs through data analysis, employee feedback, and consultation with department leaders; develop targeted learning solutions that address identified gaps Assign specialized training to Facilities Management staff using the university Learning Management System, track participant progress, and provide data analytics and completion reports to department leadership Develop training materials, Standard Operating Procedures, job aids, and reference guides that support ongoing learning and reinforce key human resources concepts in accessible, practical formats Evaluate the effectiveness of training programs through participant feedback, performance outcomes, and other metrics; continuously improve content and delivery based on results Partner with Facilities Management leadership to develop and maintain a comprehensive annual training calendar aligned with institutional priorities and compliance requirements Maintain knowledge of trends as it related to human resources employment law, best practices, and workforce development; integrate updated knowledge into training content and departmental guidance Actively participate in internal and external professional development opportunities to maintain and expand expertise Recruitment and Talent Acquisition – 25% Manage all aspects of full-cycle recruitment for assigned departments across all employee classifications — including EHRA , SHRA , temporary, student, and biweekly positions Partner with hiring managers to develop accurate job descriptions that reflect position requirements, attract qualified candidates, and align with university classification standards Work closely with the Classification and Compensation team to finalize and post new and revised positions Submit and route vacancy notices through the internal talent acquisition system, ensuring all required documentation flows through proper approval channels — including budget office and vice chancellor review — and tracking each posting through completion Screen and evaluate candidates using legally compliant selection practices; schedule interviews and actively participate in the selection process Provide hiring managers with interview best practices, structured interview questions, and evaluation criteria to support fair and effective selection decisions Ensure a professional and positive candidate application and interview experience Support all hiring actions accurately and efficiently, ensuring proper documentation, background check coordination, and onboarding preparation for selected candidates Ensure all recruitment activities comply with applicable federal and state employment laws, EEO requirements, and university policies Employee Recognition – 10% Design, implement, and manage a variety of employee recognition programs that celebrate achievement, promote morale, and reinforce a culture of appreciation and belonging Collaborate with department leaders and the Office of Human Resources staff to identify recognition opportunities and ensure programs are equitable, meaningful, and aligned with institutional values Evaluate the effectiveness of recognition initiatives regularly and recommend enhancements to keep programs fresh, relevant, and impactful Coordinate recognition events, communications, and award presentations in collaboration with the Facilities Management team File, Record, and Report Management – 10% Maintain the confidentiality and integrity of departmental personnel files in compliance with applicable privacy laws and university policy Coordinate the timely and accurate transfer of personnel information to the Office of Human Resources for inclusion in official employee records Oversee the maintenance of EHRA , SHRA , temporary, student, and biweekly employee files, ensuring completeness and accuracy Compile and prepare personnel data reports to support departmental financial forecasting, budget planning and workforce analysis This position is Mandatory Personnel: Employees whose presence has been determined to be mandatory to University operations during certain types of adverse weather or emergency events. Management Preference Substantial human resources knowledge and experience working in a large, complex organization Working knowledge of all aspects of human resources processes and procedures, including recruitment, classification, compensation, policy administration, organizational development, organizational culture, and HR information systems Highly skilled and experienced using online employment systems, Adobe, Banner HR, and the array of Office 365 products Excellent written and verbal communication skills Excellent organizational and problem-solving skills Ability to work independently and in collaboration with team members 2–5 years of human resources experience at a university or State of North Carolina agency Lic or Certification required by statute or regulation Posting Information Job Opening Date 07/20/2026 Job Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Posting Category Professional Posting Number EPA01155 Quick Link to Posting https://jobs.uncp.edu/postings/13528 Special Instructions to Applicants This position is subject to the successful completion of an employment background check. An employment background check includes a criminal background check, employment verification, reference checks, license verification (if applicable) and credit history check (if applicable). In compliance with federal law, all persons hired will be required to verify identity and eligibility to work in the United States and to complete the required employment eligibility verification form upon hire. New employees are paid only by direct deposit to the financial institution of their choice. Candidates claiming Veterans Preference must attach a copy of their DD-214 as a part of the online application process. UNC Pembroke is an Equal Opportunity Employer. The University prohibits discrimination against qualified individuals based on their status as protected veterans or individuals with disabilities, and prohibits discrimination against all individuals based on their age, race, color, genetic information, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression and national origin. UNC Pembroke is a VEVRAA Federal Contractor and seeks priority referrals of protected veterans for our openings. Applicant Documents Required Documents C V/Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Other Document Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Agency Referral American Librarian Association (ALA) Association of Fundraising Professionals BlacksInHigherEd.com Career Builder Chronicle of Higher Education Cosida CUPA HR Disabled in Higher Ed Disability Website (Other) Educause Glassdoor HigherEdJobs Indeed Inside Higher Ed Journal of Blacks in Higher Education LinkedIn Monster NACUBO NativeAmericansInHigherEd.com Native Hire NCAA Market NC Works Online / One Stop Center Newspaper Personal Referral Placement Exchange SACUBO Society of Human Resources Management (SHRM) StudentAffairs.com UNC Collaborative Website UNC Pembroke Online Employment System Veterans Advantage Jobs & Career Network Veteran Website (Other) VeteransInHigherEd.com Vocational Rehab Women in Higher Education Website - Other * How do you ensure compliance with relevant labor laws and regulations in your compensation practices? (Open Ended Question) * How many years of experience do you have in this type of position? 0-1 1-3 3-5 5-7 7+ * Do you have experience working with Banner or a similar student information system?  If so, what system(s) (Open Ended Question) * Please describe in detail your experience working in Human Resources. (Open Ended Question) CAMPUS DIRECTORY | ASK UNCP | UNIVERSITY CALENDAR To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
